    "field": "Regional climate projection",
    "problem": "The lack of a common experimental protocol across past regional climate downscaling projects has hindered the systematic characterization of uncertainties and the transfer of knowledge, making it difficult to produce robust, comparable climate projections needed for impact studies.",
    "method": "The paper describes the Coordinated Regional Downscaling Experiment (CORDEX), a framework using a common protocol to generate large, multi-model ensembles of projections to address the need for robust uncertainty characterization and comparability across previously fragmented regional climate downscaling efforts.",
    "task": "The task is to review coordinated experimental frameworks, particularly CORDEX, for producing robust regional climate projections by downscaling global climate model outputs to better characterize uncertainties for impact studies.",
