            "target_entity_instance": "CORDEX",
            "target_entity_type": "Project",
            "paragraph": "These considerations have provided the main guidelines for the ongoing discussions on the design of the CORDEX phase II framework [2], which is currently planned to encompass two components. The first, referred to as Common Regional Experiment framework (or CORDEX-CORE), envisions the completion of a common minimum ensemble of projections for all CORDEX domains by a core set of RCMS downscaling a core set of GCMs and scenarios at nominal resolutions in the range of 10-25 km.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Flagship Pilot Studies",
            "source_entity_type": "Activity",
            "relation": "PART_OF_PROJECT",
            "target_entity_instance": "CORDEX",
            "target_entity_type": "Project",
            "paragraph": "The second component of the CORDEX phase II framework is the concept of Flagship Pilot Studies (FPSs). FPSs are intended to be frontline research projects aimed at addressing in detail targeted science questions relevant to specific regional settings.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "CORDEX ESD framework",
            "source_entity_type": "Activity",
            "relation": "PART_OF_PROJECT",
            "target_entity_instance": "CORDEX",
            "target_entity_type": "Project",
            "paragraph": "Complementing these phase II activities is the development of a CORDEX ESD framework. To date, this has occurred through a series of workshops [96] that have designed a program aimed at evaluating strengths and shortcomings of a variety of ESD methods themselves and in comparison with dynamical downscaling.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
